course: dictionary
lesson: 15059
title: Reversed: turned the other way
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Reversed is the past form of the verb «reverse», which means to go backwards or turn something the other way round. Look at the sentence to find the clue. «Sam reversed the car out of the drive.» Did Sam move forwards or backwards? Backwards, so reversed means drove backwards.
explain: Reversed can also describe something that is turned the wrong way. «Lily wrote a reversed b, so it looked like a d.» The clue is looked like a d: the letter was turned the opposite way round.
explain: Try the swap check. Put a simple word in place of reversed, such as «turned» or «backwards». «Sam turned the car out of the drive» loses the idea of going backwards, so reversed gives the exact meaning.
explain: Reversed also shows swapping. «In the play, the roles were reversed: the king became the servant and the servant became the king.» Roles reversed means people swapped places.
fact: Reversed is the past form of the verb reverse: «She reversed the car.»
fact: «Reversed» means drove backwards, or turned something the other way or to the opposite.
fact: As an adjective, «reversed» means turned backwards, upside down or the opposite way round, as in «a reversed letter».
fact: In maths, 23 reversed is 32, because the digits swap places.
fact: «Roles reversed» means people swapped places.
exercise: «The van reversed into the car park.» What does reversed mean here? | Stopped for lunch | Turned off the lights | *Drove backwards | Drove very fast
exercise: In maths, what is 23 reversed? | 233 | *32 | 2 | 23
exercise: «The teacher reversed the order of the lines.» What does reversed order mean? | Made the lines longer | *Turned the other way round, so the last line comes first | Put the lines in alphabetical order | Shuffled into a random order
test: What does «the roles were reversed» mean? | Everyone did the same job | *People swapped places | Nobody had a job to do | Ben and Ellie fell out
test: Which example shows a reversed letter? | A tall, thin letter | A letter written in bold | *A b written facing the wrong way, like a d | A letter sent in the post
exam: «The reversed digits made a new number.» What does reversed mean in this sentence? | Rubbed out | *Turned the other way round | Added together | Painted red
